### 2. Section-Specific IITB Rules Engine

#### [NEW] [section_rules.json](file:///c:/Interview%20Preparation%20Platform/data/resumes/section_rules.json)

A structured JSON file with dedicated rules per IITB resume section:

```json
{
  "experience": {
    "rules": [
      "Must follow STAR format: Situation → Task → Action → Result",
      "Lead with a strong, non-repetitive action verb (Spearheaded, Engineered, Orchestrated — not 'Worked on')",
      "Quantify impact with at least one hard metric (%, ₹, hours, users)",
      "Mention tools/technologies/frameworks used",
      "Keep to exactly 1 line per sub-point (no 2-line or 1.5-line points)",
      "For internships: specify team size, project scope, and business impact",
      "Include the client/industry context when the company name alone doesn't convey scale"
    ],
    "iitb_conventions": [
      "Most Day 1 resumes have 1-2 experience entries with 3-4 sub-points each",
      "Internship descriptions should highlight cross-functional exposure"
    ]
  },
  "project": { ... },
  "por": { ... },
  "scholastic": { ... },
  "extracurricular": { ... }
}
```

Each section will have:
- `rules`: Strict structural rules to enforce
- `iitb_conventions`: IITB-specific norms (e.g., typical section lengths, ordering conventions)

#### [MODIFY] [best_practices_rules.json](file:///c:/Interview%20Preparation%20Platform/data/resumes/best_practices_rules.json)

- Keep as the **global** rules file (applies to all sections).
- The section-specific rules will be **additive** — the LLM prompt will include both global rules + the section's specific rules for each bullet.

